--- context (Desktop 2 / Phoenix, 2026-09-06) ---
Built to isolate resolution from architecture after yolov8s@1280
(results/multi_partition_yolov8s_r1280.log) landed at only 28.0% of
nameplate -- LOWER than yolov8m's 33.1% despite yolov8s@1280's higher
GMACs/call (59.66 vs 40.6). This run uses the identical, already-quantized
models/yolov8s_cut_xint8.onnx (no requantize needed) at native 640, so any
gap between this result and yolov8s@1280 isolates the resolution change
from the architecture (yolov8s's own width/depth) itself. Zero mismatches
here -- this model's calibration recipe is the established one (see
README.md:86), not the --limit 4 throughput-only recipe used for the 1280
variant, so this fps number carries no accuracy caveat.
